      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### GPU Cost Reference\n\n| Instance | Spot | On-Demand |\n|---|---|---|\n| g5.xlarge (Tier 1/2) | ~$0.35/hr | ~$1.01/hr |\n| g5.12xlarge (Tier 3) | ~$1.90/hr | ~$5.67/hr |\n\n**Multiply by GPU node hours above.**\n\nWith KEDA scale-to-zero: cost = $0 when idle.\n\n### How Scaling Works\n\n1. **KEDA** monitors CPU activity — scales Ollama to 0 after 15 min idle\n2. **Karpenter** detects empty GPU node — terminates after 10 min\n3. **Total idle-to-zero: ~25 min**\n4. Scale up: `./scripts/scale-up.sh` → Karpenter provisions GPU node (~3 min)\n\n> **Note:** EKS Auto Mode runs Karpenter on the control plane. Native `karpenter_*` metrics are unavailable — this dashboard uses `kube-state-metrics` instead."
      },
      "title": "Cost & Scaling Info"
    }
